## 📄 File-by-File Analysis

### 1. `App.xaml` + `App.xaml.cs` — Application Entry Point

**Role:** Controls the startup flow of the whole application.

**Key Logic (`App.xaml.cs`):**
- Sets `ShutdownMode` to `OnExplicitShutdown` to prevent the app from closing when the `LoginWindow` dialog closes.
- Opens `LoginWindow` as a **modal dialog**.
- On successful login → extracts `Username` and `Token` from the login window → creates and shows `MainWindow`.
- On login cancel/failure → calls `this.Shutdown()`.
- Wraps startup in a `try/catch` to show a full error dialog on crash.

---

### 2. `LoginWindow.xaml` + `LoginWindow.xaml.cs` — Login Screen

**Role:** Authenticates the user before showing the widget.

**UI (`LoginWindow.xaml`):**
- Custom borderless window (`WindowStyle="None"`, `AllowsTransparency="True"`).
- Acrylic blur background via `WindowBlur.EnableBlur()`.
- GitHub SVG logo rendered via WPF `Path`.
- Username `TextBox` + PAT `PasswordBox` with custom styled borders.
- "Get your token here" hyperlink → opens `https://github.com/settings/tokens`.
- Error message `Border` (initially `Collapsed`).
- Green GitHub-styled Login button with hover/disabled states.
- "Remember my credentials" `CheckBox` with custom template.

**Logic (`LoginWindow.xaml.cs`):**
| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `LoadSavedCredentials()` | Reads encrypted `github_credentials.dat` and pre-fills form |
| `SaveCredentials()` | Encrypts and writes credentials to file using DPAPI |
| `DeleteSavedCredentials()` | Deletes credential file |
| `EncryptString()` / `DecryptString()` | Uses `ProtectedData` (DPAPI, `CurrentUser` scope) |
| `LoginButton_Click()` | Validates → calls `GitHubService.GetContributionsAsync()` → sets `DialogResult = true` |
| `ShowError()` / `HideError()` | Shows/hides error message border |
| `TextBox_GotFocus/LostFocus` | Manually changes border color for focus indication |

> **Security note:** Credentials are encrypted with Windows DPAPI (`DataProtectionScope.CurrentUser`), meaning they are machine- and user-specific. This is a reasonable approach for a local desktop widget.

---

### 3. `GitHubService.cs` — GitHub API Client

**Role:** Fetches contribution data from GitHub's **GraphQL API v4**.

**Models:**
```csharp
ContributionData  { TotalContributions, List<ContributionDay> Days }
ContributionDay   { DateTime Date, int Count }
```

**Method: `GetContributionsAsync()`**
- Sends a GraphQL POST to `https://api.github.com/graphql`.
- Uses `Bearer` token auth.
- Requests: `contributionCalendar → totalContributions + weeks → contributionDays (count + date)`.
- Parses via `Newtonsoft.Json` (`JObject`).
- Returns a flat `ContributionData` with all days.

> [!WARNING]
> The GraphQL query is built with **raw string interpolation** (injecting `_username` directly). This is a mild injection risk, though GitHub usernames are constrained. Consider using GraphQL **variables** instead.

> [!WARNING]
> No error handling for HTTP failure codes (non-2xx). If the API returns a 401/403, the code will likely throw a `NullReferenceException` when traversing `data["data"]["user"]`.

---

### 4. `MainWindow.xaml` + `MainWindow.xaml.cs` — Main Widget

**Role:** The primary always-visible contribution widget displayed on the desktop.

**UI (`MainWindow.xaml`):**
- 900×300 custom borderless window with acrylic blur, `ResizeMode="NoResize"`.
- Rounded border (8px corners), semi-transparent white outline.
- **Title bar** — draggable, shows title + three-dot `⋯` menu button.
- **Popup menu** (3-dot `⋯`):
  - 📌 **Pin to Top** (ToggleButton) — sets `Topmost`
  - ⚡ **Launch at Startup** (ToggleButton) — writes to Windows Registry
  - 🔄 **Refresh** — reloads data
  - ✕ **Close widget** — the ONLY way to close the window
- **Header** — username + total contribution count.
- **Month labels** — `ItemsControl` with proportional widths per month.
- **Contribution Grid** — `WrapPanel(Vertical, Height=112)` inside a fixed-width `ItemsControl` (854px), each cell is a 12×12 `Border` with colored background and tooltip.
- **Legend** — "Less ▪▪▪▪▪ More" + hint text.

**Color Scheme (GitHub-style greens):**
| Level | Color | Count Range |
|---|---|---|
| 0 | `#161b22` | 0 |
| 1 | `#0e4429` | 1–3 |
| 2 | `#006d32` | 4–6 |
| 3 | `#26a641` | 7–9 |
| 4 | `#39d353` | 10+ |

**Logic (`MainWindow.xaml.cs`):**
| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `LoadContributions()` | async — fetches data, updates UI header + grid |
| `OrganizeContributionsByWeek()` | Pads leading empty cells based on start day-of-week |
| `GenerateMonthLabels()` | Calculates per-month label widths in pixels |
| `GetColorForCount()` | Maps count → color brush |
| `OnClosing()` / `Window_Closing` | Blocks all close attempts unless `_allowClose = true` |
| `SyncMenuToggles()` | Refreshes toggle states without firing their events |
| `MenuClose_Click()` | Sets `_allowClose = true` → calls `Close()` |

---

### 5. `StartupManager.cs` — Windows Startup Registry Manager

**Role:** Registers/unregisters the app in Windows startup via the Registry.

**Key:**
```
HKCU\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Run
"GitHubContributionWidget" = "\"<path-to-exe>\""
```

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `IsStartupEnabled()` | Checks if registry key exists and has a value |
| `SetStartup(bool)` | Adds or removes the registry entry |

> [!NOTE]
> Uses `Assembly.GetExecutingAssembly().Location` to get the `.exe` path, which works correctly for .NET Framework WPF apps.

---

### 6. `WindowBlur.cs` — Acrylic Window Blur

**Role:** Applies Windows Acrylic blur behind the window via P/Invoke.

**Mechanism:**
- Calls `SetWindowCompositionAttribute` from `user32.dll`.
- Sets `AccentState = ACCENT_ENABLE_ACRYLICBLURBEHIND` with `GradientColor = 0x99000000` (60% black, in `AABBGGRR` format).

> [!NOTE]
> This Win32 API (`WCA_ACCENT_POLICY`) is an undocumented/private API. It works on Windows 10/11 but may break on future Windows versions.

---

## 📦 NuGet Dependencies

| Package | Version | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `Newtonsoft.Json` | 13.0.4 | JSON parsing of GitHub API responses |
| `System.IO` | 4.3.0 | Polyfill (likely redundant on .NET 4.8.1) |
| `System.Net.Http` | 4.3.4 | `HttpClient` (likely redundant on .NET 4.8.1) |
| `System.Runtime` | 4.3.0 | Runtime polyfill |
| `System.Security.Cryptography.*` | 4.3.x | Crypto polyfills |
| `System.Security.Cryptography.ProtectedData` | 10.0.3 | DPAPI for credential encryption |

> [!TIP]
> Several polyfill packages (`System.IO`, `System.Net.Http`, `System.Runtime`, `System.Security.Cryptography.*`) are unnecessary on .NET 4.8.1 since those APIs are built into the framework. They can be safely removed to reduce package bloat.

