## 🏛️ Architecture Summary

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[App.xaml.cs\nStartup] -->|ShowDialog| B[LoginWindow]
    B -->|Validates via| C[GitHubService\nGraphQL API]
    B -->|DialogResult=true| D[MainWindow]
    D -->|Loads data via| C
    D -->|EnableBlur| E[WindowBlur\nP/Invoke]
    D -->|Read/Write| F[StartupManager\nRegistry]
    B -->|Encrypt/Save| G[github_credentials.dat\nDPAPI]
```

---

## ⚠️ Issues & Observations

| # | Severity | Issue |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | 🔴 High | `GitHubService` has no HTTP error handling — non-2xx responses cause unhandled `NullReferenceException` |
| 2 | 🟡 Medium | GraphQL query uses string interpolation for username — prefer GraphQL variables |
| 3 | 🟡 Medium | `MainWindow` always forces startup registration on load (`if (!IsStartupEnabled()) SetStartup(true)`) — user can't permanently disable startup |
| 4 | 🟡 Medium | `Class1.cs` is referenced in `.csproj` but file is missing from the root — will cause build error |
| 5 | 🟠 Low | Redundant NuGet polyfill packages that aren't needed on .NET 4.8.1 |
| 6 | 🟠 Low | `README.md` is essentially empty (26 bytes) |
| 7 | 🟠 Low | `WindowBlur` uses an undocumented Win32 API — may break on future Windows versions |
| 8 | 🟠 Low | Credentials file (`github_credentials.dat`) is saved in the current working directory — consider using `%APPDATA%` instead |
| 9 | 🟠 Low | `ContributionGrid` has a hardcoded `Width="854"` — not responsive |

---

## ✅ What's Done Well

- Clean separation between Login, Main UI, API service, and helpers.
- Credential security using Windows DPAPI (user-scoped, machine-tied).
- "Close blocking" pattern in `MainWindow` to prevent accidental closure.
- GitHub-accurate contribution color scale.
- Smooth acrylic glass UI matching GitHub's dark design language.
- Correct async/await usage in `LoadContributions` and `LoginButton_Click`.
- Startup registry management cleanly abstracted in `StartupManager`.
